{"id": 25, "ts": 1783910516.5334418, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I appreciate Sofia\u2019s request for more concrete evidence on stress handling and technical ability, especially for Candidates\u202fB and\u202fD. From the assessment notes we now have, Candidate\u202fB does indeed handle stress very well and shows solid technical competence through his weather\u2011assessment skill and excellent computer abilities. However, his tendency to make nasty remarks toward colleagues signals serious crew\u2011cooperation and professional\u2011communication concerns, which are critical for long\u2011haul cockpit harmony. Candidate\u202fD responds adequately to unexpected events and demonstrates strong problem\u2011solving, concentration, and responsibility\u2014indicating good technical competence\u2014but his \u201cknow\u2011it\u2011all\u201d attitude and hot temper raise similar cooperation and communication red flags, and we lack clear evidence of strong stress resilience.\nGiven that both B and D have notable interpersonal weaknesses that could undermine crew safety, while Candidate\u202fA still offers proven 100\u202f% reliability and a positive crew atmosphere (despite the missing stress\u2011resilience data), I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fA is the best overall fit at this stage. I will continue to monitor any new information on A\u2019s stress handling, but based on the current evidence, my provisional recommendation stays with Candidate\u202fA."}
